@page "/workforce"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@*
    Product.razor - route /workforce
    ------------------------------------------------------------------------
    A faithful build of the reference Product page, using Polypus branding:

      1. Hero with the "not tools, a Product" statement plus a small
         Select -> Deploy -> Get flow diagram
      2. Three feature rows - Skills, Agents, Product - each with a button
         to its page
      3. The Product bundles grid (Invoice Processing ... Contract Accounting),
         with the not-yet-available bundles marked "Coming soon"
      4. Build Your Own band
      5. The "can help you scale" statement
      6. The five reference questions, using the shared FaqList accordion

    Copy is carried verbatim from the reference; only the brand name is swapped
    (Hypatos -> Polypus). Styling is scoped in Product.razor.css and uses the
    Polypus design tokens, so nothing here copies the reference theme.

    Linked from: the header "Product" menu.
*@

<PageTitle>Product - Polypus</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="A team of Polypus agents that runs document-heavy finance and operations processes from intake to a controlled action in your system of record." />
</HeadContent>

@* ==========================================================================
   1. Hero
   ========================================================================== *@
<section class="section wf-hero">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="wf-hero__inner">
            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">Inside the Agentic GBS Product</p>
                <h1 class="display wf-hero__title">Not AI tools. A GBS Product.</h1>
                <p class="wf-hero__copy">
                    Working with us is like hiring. Tell us which tasks need handling - validation,
                    matching, prediction, compliance - and we'll bring you the Agents to execute them.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="wf-flow" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="wf-flow__step">
                    <span class="wf-flow__icon"><AppIcon Name="sparkle" Size="18" /></span>
                    <span>
                        <span class="wf-flow__kicker">What you select</span>
                        <span class="wf-flow__label">Skills</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
                <div class="wf-flow__line"></div>
                <div class="wf-flow__step">
                    <span class="wf-flow__icon"><AppIcon Name="user-check" Size="18" /></span>
                    <span>
                        <span class="wf-flow__kicker">What we deploy</span>
                        <span class="wf-flow__label">Agents</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
                <div class="wf-flow__line"></div>
                <div class="wf-flow__step wf-flow__step--accent">
                    <span class="wf-flow__icon"><AppIcon Name="users" Size="18" /></span>
                    <span>
                        <span class="wf-flow__kicker">What you get</span>
                        <span class="wf-flow__label">Product</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

@* ==========================================================================
   2. Feature rows
   ========================================================================== *@
<section class="section section--paper-alt">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="wf-feature">
            <div class="wf-feature__copy">
                <p class="wf-feature__kicker">What You Select</p>
                <h2 class="wf-feature__title">Skills</h2>
                <p class="wf-feature__copy">Select the GBS Skills your process needs to cover.</p>
                <div class="wf-feature__action">
                    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/skills">
                        Go to GBS Skills
                        <AppIcon Name="arrow-right" Size="17" />
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="wf-diagram" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="wf-diagram__node"><AppIcon Name="shield-check" Size="17" /> Input validation</span>
                <span class="wf-diagram__node"><AppIcon Name="search" Size="17" /> Information extraction</span>
                <span class="wf-diagram__node"><AppIcon Name="layers" Size="17" /> Document classification</span>
                <span class="wf-diagram__node"><AppIcon Name="check-circle" Size="17" /> Duplicate prevention</span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="wf-feature wf-feature--reverse">
            <div class="wf-feature__copy">
                <p class="wf-feature__kicker">What We Deploy</p>
                <h2 class="wf-feature__title">Agents</h2>
                <p class="wf-feature__copy">We staff GBS Agents that match your Skills picks.</p>
                <div class="wf-feature__action">
                    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/agents">
                        Go to GBS Agents
                        <AppIcon Name="arrow-right" Size="17" />
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="wf-diagram" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="wf-diagram__node"><AppIcon Name="user-check" Size="17" /> Collaborate</span>
                <span class="wf-diagram__node"><AppIcon Name="sparkle" Size="17" /> Reason</span>
                <span class="wf-diagram__node"><AppIcon Name="plug" Size="17" /> Use tools</span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="wf-feature">
            <div class="wf-feature__copy">
                <p class="wf-feature__kicker">What You Get</p>
                <h2 class="wf-feature__title">Product</h2>
                <p class="wf-feature__copy">Agents with the right GBS Skills become your Product in production.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="wf-diagram" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="wf-diagram__node wf-diagram__node--hub"><AppIcon Name="users" Size="18" /> Your GBS Product</span>
                <span class="wf-diagram__node"><AppIcon Name="scan" Size="17" /> Invoice Processing</span>
                <span class="wf-diagram__node"><AppIcon Name="check-circle" Size="17" /> Order Confirmations</span>
                <span class="wf-diagram__node"><AppIcon Name="layers" Size="17" /> Delivery Notes</span>
                <span class="wf-diagram__node"><AppIcon Name="flow" Size="17" /> Order Management</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

@* ==========================================================================
   3. Product bundles
   ========================================================================== *@
<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading Eyebrow="Agentic GBS Product bundles"
                       Title="Your GBS Product"
                       Description="Start with a standard Product – trailed, tested and built agentic from the ground up for the most common GBS scenarios." />

        <div class="wf-bundles mt-7">
            @foreach (var bundle in Bundles)
            {
                <article class="wf-card @(bundle.Href is null ? "wf-card--soon" : null)">
                    <span class="wf-card__icon"><AppIcon Name="@bundle.Icon" Size="21" /></span>
                    <h3 class="wf-card__title">@bundle.Title</h3>
                    <p class="wf-card__text">@bundle.Text</p>

                    <div class="wf-card__action">
                        @if (bundle.Href is not null)
                        {
                            <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" href="@bundle.Href">
                                Explore
                                <AppIcon Name="arrow-right" Size="15" />
                            </a>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <span class="wf-card__soon">
                                <span class="badge-dot"></span>
                                Coming soon
                            </span>
                        }
                    </div>
                </article>
            }
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

@* ==========================================================================
   4. Build Your Own
   ========================================================================== *@
<section class="section section--flush">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="wf-build">
            <div>
                <h2>Build Your Own</h2>
                <p>Create your own Product directly on the Polypus platform.</p>

                <ul class="wf-build__points">
                    <li><AppIcon Name="check" Size="15" /> Custom workflows</li>
                    <li><AppIcon Name="check" Size="15" /> Process-specific skills</li>
                    <li><AppIcon Name="check" Size="15" /> Tailored agents</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="wf-build__action">
                <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact">
                    Talk to us
                    <AppIcon Name="arrow-right" Size="18" />
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

@* ==========================================================================
   5. Scale band
   ========================================================================== *@
<section class="section section--paper-alt">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="wf-scale">
            <h2>An Agentic GBS Product that can help you scale</h2>
            <p>
                Deploy seamless Agentic workflows across every major GBS pillar: from procurement and
                sales to accounts payable and receivable. The Polypus Agentic GBS Product has
                built-in controls, explainable decisions and is easily scalable. Meaning you can
                release human capacity to focus on tasks that only people can do.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

@* ==========================================================================
   6. Frequently Asked Questions
   ========================================================================== *@
<section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
        <SectionHeading Eyebrow="Questions" Title="Frequently Asked Questions" Align="center" />
        <FaqList Items="Questions" CssClass="mt-7" />
    </div>
</section>

@code {
    /// <summary>One bundle card. A null Href means the bundle is not available yet.</summary>
    private sealed record Bundle(string Title, string Text, string Icon, string? Href);

    private static readonly Bundle[] Bundles =
    [
        new("Invoice Processing", "A Product that captures, codes, matches and validates every invoice.", "scan", "/workforce/invoice-processing"),
        new("Order Confirmations", "A Product catching and matching every line, price, and quantity.", "check-circle", "/workforce/order-confirmations"),
        new("Delivery Notes", "A Product turning delivery notes into validated receipts.", "layers", "/workforce/delivery-notes"),
        new("Order Management", "A Product validating sales orders against catalogue, pricing, volume.", "flow", "/workforce/order-management"),
        new("Dunning Letters", "A Product that captures, matches and resolves every dunning letter.", "mail", null),
        new("Cash Application", "A Product that matches incoming payments to open receivables.", "chart", null),
        new("Contract Accounting", "A Product that keeps contract terms and postings aligned.", "building", null)
    ];

    /// <summary>The five questions from the reference Product page, carried verbatim.</summary>
    private static readonly IReadOnlyList<Faq> Questions =
    [
        new Faq
        {
            Category = "Product",
            Question = "What is the difference between Skills, Agents and a Product?",
            Answer = "A skill is a pre-packaged, reusable capability, like reading a document or " +
                     "validating a field. An agent is the worker applying skills to run a process " +
                     "step and make or propose decisions. A Polypus Product is the operating layer " +
                     "above them: which agents run, what skills they have, and with which controls " +
                     "and authority."
        },
        new Faq
        {
            Category = "Product",
            Question = "Do I choose the Skills that go into a Product?",
            Answer = "You don't need to. Polypus has standard, pre-packaged Product bundles that " +
                     "already include all the necessary Skills for a process to run end to end. You " +
                     "can opt out of certain Skills if your process does not require them. E.g.: you " +
                     "already have an e-invoicing solution in place so you can go live with an " +
                     "Invoice Processing Product without an e-Invoicing skill in it."
        },
        new Faq
        {
            Category = "Product",
            Question = "Can we start with a single process?",
            Answer = "Yes. A single Product, such as for invoice processing, proves the model on " +
                     "real volume. Expanding to order confirmations or delivery notes afterwards " +
                     "reuses some of the same skills, connectors and controls, so you do not start " +
                     "from scratch when you grow."
        },
        new Faq
        {
            Category = "Product",
            Question = "What does Build Your Own Product mean?",
            Answer = "Build Your Own is the offer for documents outside the available named " +
                     "solutions. You get build access to the Polypus platform and create your own " +
                     "Product for entirely new document types, with the same controls and " +
                     "integrations available across the standard offering."
        },
        new Faq
        {
            Category = "Product",
            Question = "How does a Product keep humans in control?",
            Answer = "Every exception is logged with a specific reason and routed to a named owner. " +
                     "Approvals follow your authority rules, and each decision leaves a trail: what " +
                     "the agent read, what it decided, and what the system of record did. Reviewers " +
                     "work in the review console, the human-in-the-loop interface where people see " +
                     "each case, decide, and have their revision recorded."
        }
    ];
}

